      "mentions": 32,
      "title": {
        "en": "Dedicated emergency doctors with billing friction"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents highlight the skill of emergency clinicians and ICU nurses who stabilized critically injured pets and saved animals from severe trauma. However, client sentiment is mixed due to complaints regarding front-desk interactions, where multiple reviewers perceived reception staff as indifferent or overly focused on collecting payments."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "prices",
      "sentiment": "negative",
      "mentions": 25,
      "title": {
        "en": "High emergency bills and upfront deposits"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pricing is the primary source of client dissatisfaction. Reviewers report steep fees for emergency consultations and overnight hospitalization, with quotes reaching several thousand dollars. Many owners express frustration that substantial financial deposits were required before clinical treatments or diagnostic evaluations began."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 20,
      "title": {
        "en": "Advanced trauma stabilization alongside tragic outcomes"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Emergency outcomes vary widely according to medical severity. Many clients credit the ICU and surgical teams with saving pets following severe bite wounds, internal bleeding, and neurological distress. Conversely, families dealing with critical terminal crises express deep distress over rapid clinical decline and perceived diagnostic delays."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Is the hospital open twenty-four hours for pet emergencies?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, LAASER operates around the clock every day of the week to handle urgent and critical animal emergencies."
      },
      "basis": "both"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "How are patient admissions and emergency triage handled?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Critically ill animals are triaged upon arrival, but non-critical cases may experience lengthy lobby waits depending on hospital caseload."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "What deposit policies apply to emergency treatments?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Clients report that substantial upfront deposits or full treatment estimates must be authorized before inpatient procedures begin."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "What specialty services are available at LAASER?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "The facility offers emergency trauma care, internal medicine, surgery, diagnostic imaging, and physical rehabilitation."
      },
      "basis": "both"
    }
